Axe-core scans
--------------

@axe-core/playwright integrated into all 6 e2e specs:
  - e2e/home.spec.ts
  - e2e/cursor-happy-path.spec.ts
  - e2e/cursor-reduced-motion.spec.ts
  - e2e/cursor-skip.spec.ts
  - e2e/cursor-mobile.spec.ts
  - e2e/cursor-api-down.spec.ts

Tag set: wcag2a, wcag2aa, wcag21a, wcag21aa.
Final-state scans: 0 violations across all 6 specs.

Two real product violations were surfaced and fixed in task 048:

1. Skip-link contrast (cursor-mobile, wcag2aa color-contrast)
   - Before: text-white/80 on bg-black/40 → contrast ratio 2.38:1.
   - After: text-white on bg-black/80 with border-white/40 → contrast > 4.5:1.
   - File: src/components/cursor/skip-link.tsx.

2. Mobile router teardown leak (cursor-mobile)
   - Before: CinematicIntroMobile rendered <Hero /> on its `hero` beat but
     never told the router the cinematic was finished, so the router-level
     <SkipLink /> stayed mounted on top of the hero forever on mobile.
   - After: CinematicIntroMobile fires
     `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("blueprint:cinematic-complete"))`
     on the first render of the `hero` beat. CinematicRouter listens (T015)
     and flips its `mode` to "hero", which drops the SkipLink overlay.
   - File: src/components/cursor/cinematic-intro-mobile.tsx.
   - cursor-mobile spec now also asserts `getByRole("button", { name: "Skip
     cinematic intro" }).toHaveCount(0)` after the mobile cinematic finishes.

Keyboard walkthrough
--------------------

`npm run dev`, `/en`, default desktop motion:

1. Page loads. Initial focus on document body.
2. Tab → focus moves to the SkipLink button (fixed bottom-right).
   - aria-label "Skip cinematic intro" announced (NVDA on Windows).
   - Visible focus ring (`focus-visible:ring-2 ring-white ring-offset-2
     ring-offset-black`) renders against the dark backdrop.
3. Shift+Tab → focus returns to body. No tab stops between body and skip
   link in the cinematic state.
4. Press Enter on the skip button → CinematicRouter receives
   `blueprint:cinematic-skip`, swaps to <Hero />.
5. Tab → focus lands on the ReplayButton inside the hero.
   - aria-label "Replay cinematic intro" announced.
   - Visible focus ring renders against the black hero background.
6. Hero h1 ("Built by the process it teaches.") is announced when
   navigating by heading (H key in NVDA).
7. Hero metadata <p> is read in reading order after the h1.
8. Reduced-motion path (`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`): no skip link,
   role=status notice "Cinematic intro disabled per your motion
   preferences." announced as a status message.

No keyboard traps observed in any path.

Screen reader spot-check
------------------------

NVDA on Windows, Firefox, /en:
  - h1 ("Built by the process it teaches.") announced.
  - metadata line ("commit ... · N specs · N tasks · 0 lies") announced.
  - replay button announced with aria-label "Replay cinematic intro".

All clear.
